- kb/notes/the-practical-scheduler-is-the-host-language.md — The practical scheduler is the host language, not a reified select — The simplest practical orchestration library demotes the tool loop to a returning, per-call-parameterized function and lets ordinary host-language code play select and K — reifying K only when the run must outlive its process or outgrow its memory
